 After all chapters merge, a **full-book continuity audit** runs before final review. The auditor processes every chapter sequentially, building a cumulative world state and flagging long-range contradictions, unresolved plot threads, and accumulated drift that per-chapter checks can't catch. Results are compiled into `notes/continuity-audit-report.md`.
 
+### Release Phase
+
+Final review no longer ends the pipeline. Once word counts are tallied it moves the project to `PACKAGING` and hands off to the **packager**, which assembles `manuscript/manuscript.md` and `release/manifest.json`. On success the project moves to `RELEASING` and the **marketer** produces `release/listing.json`. That listing is validated against the KDP release policy — a valid listing ends the project `RELEASED`, a missing or invalid one ends it `FAILED`.
